{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"0d8d0751-4731-47ab-98b2-4fa50fbc35c8","title":"A system of two linear equations as crossing lines"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0d8d0751-4731-47ab-98b2-4fa50fbc35c8","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Each linear equation draws a line. A solution to the system must lie on both lines at once.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Two equations, one shared point"},{"op":"equation","id":"eqone","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=x+1"},{"op":"figure","id":"graph","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-1,5],"y":[-1,6],"axes":"edge","x_label":"x","y_label":"y"},"marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"lineone","y":"x+1","domain":[-1,5],"label":"y = x + 1"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0d8d0751-4731-47ab-98b2-4fa50fbc35c8","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Now add the second equation. The crossing is the only point that belongs to both lines.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"eqtwo","anchor":{"el":"eqone","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=-x+5"},{"op":"figure","id":"secondline","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"fn","id":"linetwo","y":"-x+5","domain":[-1,5],"label":"y = −x + 5"},{"kind":"point","id":"crossing","at":{"hit":["lineone","linetwo"]}}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What must be true about the coordinates of the crossing point?","expected_gist":"They satisfy both equations at the same time."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0d8d0751-4731-47ab-98b2-4fa50fbc35c8","step":{"id":"s3","script":"At the crossing, both expressions give the same y. Set them equal to find x, then substitute to find y.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"solve","anchor":{"el":"eqtwo","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x+1=-x+5\\;\\Rightarrow\\;2x=4\\;\\Rightarrow\\;x=2"},{"op":"equation","id":"substitute","anchor":{"el":"solve","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"y=2+1=3"},{"op":"figure","id":"guides","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"crossing"},"to":[2,0],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"crossing"},"to":[0,3],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"text","at":[2.65,3.25],"text":"(2, 3)"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"0d8d0751-4731-47ab-98b2-4fa50fbc35c8","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Check the point in both equations. Both are true, so two, three is the solution to the system.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"check","anchor":{"el":"substitute","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"3=2+1\\qquad 3=-2+5"},{"op":"figure","id":"solutionmark","on":"graph","marks":[{"kind":"circle","center":{"at":"crossing"},"r":0.22},{"kind":"text","at":[3.1,2.5],"text":"solution","size":"small"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
